  "content": {
    "id": "p25-q10-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "10",
    "prompt": "A sequence is defined by $t_n=5^n+2^{n-1}$.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p25-q10a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "Find $t_1$, $t_2$, and $t_3$.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$t_1=6$, $t_2=27$, $t_3=129$.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}t_1&=5^1+2^0=6\\\\t_2&=5^2+2^1=27\\\\t_3&=5^3+2^2=129\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 28
      },
      {
        "id": "p25-q10b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "Suggest a positive integer greater than 1 that divides every term in this sequence.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$3$.",
          "worked": "$6=3\\times2$, $27=3\\times9$ and $129=3\\times43$, suggesting that $3$ divides every term.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 12
      },
      {
        "id": "p25-q10c",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": "Prove by mathematical induction that your conjecture in part (b) is correct.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": {
            "format": "maths-editor-document-v1",
            "version": 1,
            "blocks": [
              {
                "id": "p25-q10c-short-result",
                "type": "paragraph",
                "fontSize": null,
                "align": "left",
                "spaceBefore": 0,
                "spaceAfter": 2,
                "lineHeight": 1.4,
                "indent": 0,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "type": "math",
                    "latex": "3\\mid(5^n+2^{n-1})",
                    "display": false
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": " for every positive integer ",
                    "marks": []
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "math",
                    "latex": "n",
                    "display": false
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": ".",
                    "marks": []
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "id": "p25-q10c-short-method",
                "type": "paragraph",
                "fontSize": null,
                "align": "left",
                "spaceBefore": 0,
                "spaceAfter": 2,
                "lineHeight": 1.4,
                "indent": 0,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Check ",
                    "marks": []
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "math",
                    "latex": "t_1=6",
                    "display": false
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "; assuming ",
                    "marks": []
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "math",
                    "latex": "t_k=3m",
                    "display": false
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": ", obtain ",
                    "marks": []
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "math",
                    "latex": "t_{k+1}=3(5m-2^{k-1})",
                    "display": false
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": ".",
                    "marks": []
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          "worked": "Let $P(n)$ state that $5^n+2^{n-1}$ is divisible by $3$.\n\nBase case: $t_1=5+1=6$, which is divisible by $3$.\n\nInductive hypothesis: assume $P(k)$ is true for some positive integer $k$. Then $5^k+2^{k-1}=3m$ for an integer $m$.\n\nInductive step:\n$$\\begin{align*}t_{k+1}&=5^{k+1}+2^k\\\\t_{k+1}&=5\\cdot5^k+2\\cdot2^{k-1}\\\\t_{k+1}&=5(3m-2^{k-1})+2\\cdot2^{k-1}\\\\t_{k+1}&=15m-3\\cdot2^{k-1}\\\\t_{k+1}&=3(5m-2^{k-1}).\\end{align*}$$\nSince $5m-2^{k-1}$ is an integer, $t_{k+1}$ is divisible by $3$. Thus $P(k+1)$ is true.\n\nTherefore, by mathematical induction, $3$ divides $t_n$ for every positive integer $n$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 108
      },
      {
        "id": "p25-q10d",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "d",
        "prompt": "If you are familiar with modular arithmetic, then supply a quick proof that your conjecture in part (b) is correct.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$5^n+2^{n-1}\\equiv 3\\cdot2^{n-1}\\equiv0\\pmod3$, since $5\\equiv2\\pmod3$.",
          "worked": "Since $5\\equiv2\\pmod3$,\n$$\\begin{align*}5^n+2^{n-1}&\\equiv2^n+2^{n-1}\\pmod3\\\\5^n+2^{n-1}&\\equiv2^{n-1}(2+1)\\pmod3\\\\5^n+2^{n-1}&\\equiv3\\cdot2^{n-1}\\pmod3\\\\5^n+2^{n-1}&\\equiv0\\pmod3.\\end{align*}$$\nTherefore every term is divisible by $3$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 52
      }
    ]
  },
